<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nguyễn Lữ</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1754">1754</a>–<a href="/years/1787">1787</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nguyễn Lữ was the youngest of the three <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tay-son-dynasty">Tây Sơn</a> brothers who rose against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguyen-lords">Nguyễn lords</a> in 1771, together with Nguyễn Nhạc and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quang-trung">Nguyễn Huệ</a>. After their victories he was given a royal title and responsibility for the far south, but he proved a weaker commander than his brothers and lost ground to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gia-long">Nguyễn Ánh</a>. He died around 1787.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nguyen-lu.jpg" alt="Nguyễn Lữ" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 唐吉訶德的侍從 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nguyen_Lu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
